    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0768" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/668: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-24T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 26—10:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>64. My 61 of December 22, 5 p.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d613-f1"/> Law number 56
                    approving modifications introduced by the U.S. in the treaty of April 6, 1914,
                        <pb facs="0769" n="645" xml:id="pg645"/> was signed by Executive and
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs today, the 24th instant.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d613-f2"/> Article 2 of this law is embodied in Spanish text of
                    enclosure number 3 with my despatch number 727 of October 17 last<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d613-f3"/> and I request that Department delay preparation of our
                    exchange copy of ratification pending my further consultation with Colombian
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d613-f1" n="10" xml:id="d613-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d613-f2" n="11" xml:id="d613-f2-content">
                <p>The modified treaty was presented to the Colombian Congress Aug. 20, 1921, and
                    approved by it on Dec. 22.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d613-f3" n="12" xml:id="d613-f3-content">
